# NomadicOS — Environment Variables (BP §103)

Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env`.

```bash
# Deployment
NOMADICOS_ENV=development

# PostgreSQL (ADR-0031: local dev database via docker-compose.dev.yml)
# The dev database runs in Docker: port 5433 on Windows -> 5432 inside.
# Set POSTGRES_PASSWORD to the password of the nomadicos role.
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5433
POSTGRES_DB=nomadicos
POSTGRES_USER=nomadicos
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me

# Enable PostgreSQL as the durable source of truth for local development
# (SPEC §34). Set to "file" to use the deterministic file adapter instead.
NOMADICOS_PERSISTENCE_BACKEND=postgres

# Local data
NOMADICOS_DATA_DIR=./data            # vector data, artifacts, backups (ADR-0008)
NOMADICOS_MODEL_DIR=./models         # local GGUF model artifacts (ADR-0005)

# Logging
NOMADICOS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
```

Rules (BP §103, ADR-0021):

- Environment variables carry deployment-level settings only — not application policy,
  not secrets-at-rest.
- Real secrets go to Windows Credential Manager / DPAPI via SecretManager; the
  encrypted-file store is the portable fallback.
- Never log secrets; redaction list per BP §256 is enforced centrally.
